# Recovery Procedure: {{ device.vendor }} {{ device.model }}

**Device ID:** `{{ device.id }}`
**External Programmer Supported:** {{ device.blockers.recovery.external_programmer }}
**Notes:** {{ device.blockers.recovery.notes }}

## 1. Preparation

1. Remove AC power and all batteries. Wait 10 seconds.
2. Verify the programmer VCC voltage is **3.3 V** (or **1.8 V** with level shifter if applicable).
3. Verify the SHA-256 checksum of your stored original vendor backup before writing.

## 2. Restore Original Vendor Firmware

{% if dual_chip %}
Write the verified bottom (8 MiB) and top (4 MiB) backups back to their respective chips:

```bash
flashrom -p <programmer> -w bottom1.bin
flashrom -p <programmer> -w top1.bin
```
{% else %}
Write the verified full vendor backup back to the SPI flash chip:

```bash
flashrom -p <programmer> -w {{ device.id }}_full_backup.rom
```
{% endif %}

4. Disconnect the clip, reconnect power, and confirm the vendor firmware boots normally.
